// Title: Windows Credential Manager Access via VaultCmd
// Sigma ID: 58f50261-c53b-4c88-bd12-1d71f12eda4c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-04-08 | Modified: 2022-05-13
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1555.004
// Description: List credentials currently stored in Windows Credential Manager via the native Windows utility
//   vaultcmd.exe
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1555.004/T1555.004.md#atomic-test-1---access-saved-credentials-via-vaultcmd
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_vaultcmd_list_creds.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\VaultCmd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "VAULTCMD.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains "/listcreds:"
